  "decisionSummary": "The dev-publish v11/0.0.11 source is canonical. v10/0.0.10 installed and pinned correctly on us.paype.cc and NEVER ran: it received the platform per-grain key correctly ('jinn: keybox derivation = platform-grain-v1') and then looped forever on 'keybox open: keybox: save: keybox: atomically publish retained temporary file: no such file or directory', with the grain's storage holding only .keybox.lock, grain-id and grain-type. The cause was in the SHARED grain-crypto-journal submodule, not in Jinn: a first save published by linking through /proc/self/fd/<n>, and a production grain has no /proc because sandstorm's backend.c++ passes the supervisor's --proc flag only inside 'if (devMode)'. The existing-destination path uses RENAME_EXCHANGE and was unaffected, which is why only first saves broke. This cut points the submodule at grain-crypto-journal 3610213, which renames the named temporary instead.",
  "internalControls": {
    "status": "passed",
    "checks": [
      "clean tracked dev-publish source at the selected commit; make test green and make pack clean",
      "two INDEPENDENT fresh recursive clones at DIFFERENT paths (/home/user/Desktop/jinn11A and /home/user/Desktop/jinn11-repro-B) produced identical packages: packageId 96053cae9d4153bc59388958222b57d3, sha256 96053cae9d4153bc59388958222b57d3c579dae960a380698a20198375431e8b",
      "reproducibility confirmed independently of the packer's own report: sha256sum on both files matched and cmp reported identical bytes",
      "the component fix carries its own guard: TestFirstSavePublishesVerifiedInode pins that a first save completes, publishes the exact bytes with no surviving temporary, and that a second save still works through the RENAME_EXCHANGE path",
      "HONEST LIMIT ON THAT GUARD: it cannot reproduce the original failure, because a developer workstation always has /proc \u2014 which is exactly why this bug survived local testing. The decisive control is a live grain.",
      "my first root-cause claim (a missing CAP_DAC_READ_SEARCH) was DISPROVED by running the keybox suite unprivileged, and corrected in C-066 before any code was changed",
      "the release cohort guard pins appId, packageId, name and version together; all advanced, and its pkgdef assertion now derives from wantVersionN rather than hardcoding a second copy of the number",
      "STILL OWED: governed publication, then a clean-tenant fresh-grain runtime proof at v11. This receipt does not claim it."
    ]
  },
